2- Microsoft TRELLIS (and TRELLIS 2 / ComfyUI-TRELLIS)Best for: Overall geometric fidelity, complex topologies, and PBR textures.Why it shines: TRELLIS uses Structured Latents (SLAT). Instead of creating "melted" voxel meshes, it handles thin structures, complex silhouettes, and intricate geometry dramatically better than older generators. It outputs .glb or .obj meshes along with 3D Gaussian Splats.   Tencent Hunyuan3D 2.0 / 2.1 (via ComfyUI-Hunyuan3D-Wrapper)Best for: Fast text/image-to-3D with dedicated texture synthesis (Hunyuan3D-Paint).   Why it shines: It excels at generating stylized objects and game props with clean texture projection.Hi3D / TripoSR (Lightweight alternatives)Useful for ultra-fast coarse meshes or low-VRAM environments.The ComfyUI AdvantageInstead of relying on a closed service's internal text-to-image engine, you can generate an exact concept art angle using FLUX or SDXL with ControlNet / LoRAs, pass it to an automatic background-removal node (like BRIA RMBG), feed that mask straight into TRELLIS, and write the finished .glb to your shared cloud volume for Blender.   

